{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#3151","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#3151","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#3151\",\"parent_revision\":\"3baac791cbd6bdef9266d6c9596d8613283a25c5\",\"root_revision\":\"644d298a2a0cd2e0424d3eedd18afaed326e72c118ef0524db1a675114f2a5fd\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: P1\\ntype: Refactor\\nstatus: open\\nadded: 2026-08-22\\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nA SAM task is not a file. It is an entry in the configured backend, read and written programmatically through the MCP operations or the CLI, addressed as `P{id}/T{id}`. It is never read or written by a file operation.\\n\\nThe plugin's own content still says otherwise in 138 places \u2014 92 in markdown, 46 in Python under `skills/implementation-manager/scripts/`. This has been corrected by instruction repeatedly over roughly six months and has not closed.\\n\\nObserved cause: correcting the prose does not work, because two authoritative sources actively regenerate it.\\n\\nFirst, the language is a live data contract, not a wording choice. `/dh:start-task` writes a session context file whose JSON key is literally `task_file_path` and whose value is a real filesystem path. The test suite exercises it across four files:\\n\\n    {\\\"task_file_path\\\": \\\"plan/P001.yaml\\\", \\\"task_id\\\": \\\"T1\\\"}\\n    {\\\"task_file_path\\\": \\\"/tmp/plan/P001-feature.yaml\\\", \\\"task_id\\\": \\\"T1\\\", ...}\\n\\nAny agent or hook reading that payload is correct to call the thing a task file \u2014 that is what the field is named and what it holds. A partial migration also stalled here: `tests_backlog/test_high_level_storage_boundaries.py` asserts `\\\"task_file_path\\\" not in source` for one module while the key remains the contract everywhere else, which pins the inconsistency rather than closing it.\\n\\nSecond, `AGENTS.md` instructs every agent to go and learn the file-based model. Its \\\"Required Reading by Task Type\\\" section routes task work to `docs/TASK_FILE_FORMAT.md` \u2014 29K, referenced from ten documents, with a second copy at `docs/sdlc-layers/layer-0/task-file-format.md`.\\n\\nSo the loop is: an agent reads `AGENTS.md`, is told to load `TASK_FILE_FORMAT.md`, learns tasks are files, and writes that into whatever it edits \u2014 in good faith, and consistently with the live JSON key. Prose is the loop's output, so each prose-scoped correction fixes the open file and leaves the sources intact.\\n\\nImpact: agents are taught a storage model the system does not use. Concrete consequences already observed \u2014 `skills/forensic-review/SKILL.md` documents a parameter named `task_file_path`; `skills/backlog/references/item-schema.md` defines the `plan` field as \\\"relative path to SAM task file\\\"; `skills/execution/SKILL.md` has a workflow step \\\"Read Task File\\\"; `agents/code-reviewer.md` says \\\"Read the SAM task file using `mcp__plugin_dh_sam__sam_task`\\\", calling the right operation by the wrong name. A path-based handoff also silently produces an empty read in a worktree-isolated dispatch rather than an error, and on a remote backend there is no file to read at all.\\n\\n**User-provided context**: the ordering that would close it appears to be structural-first \u2014 rename the context-file key and its payload to a plan/task address, retire `TASK_FILE_FORMAT.md` and remove it from `AGENTS.md` required reading, delete the layer-0 duplicate, and only then sweep the prose, which by that point has nothing regenerating it. Recorded as a hypothesis for grooming to validate, not as a requirement.\\n\\n## Fact-Check\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-08-28T12:27:28.763362Z</sub>\\n\\n1. **VERIFIED**: `sam_schema/core/models.py` line 749 declares `task_file_path: str` as a required field in `ActiveTaskContext` (not `Task` model as phrased, but the field exists and is required in the context schema).\\n\\n2. **VERIFIED**: `memory_context_backend.py` line 59 fabricates `task_file_path=f\\\"{plan_dir}/{plan}.yaml\\\"` exactly as claimed.\\n\\n3. **VERIFIED**: `github_context_backend.py` line 181 assigns `task_file_path=_resolve_task_file_path(plan, plan_dir)`, with the function defined at lines 350-363 and documented as mirroring `LocalContextBackend._resolve_task_file_path` at line 353.\\n\\n4. **VERIFIED**: `sam_schema/core/backends/beads.py` line 1306 calls `_resolve_task_file_path(plan, plan_dir)` and the function is defined at lines 1378-1389, with comment \\\"Mirrors LocalContextBackend pattern\\\" at line 1379. This pattern is identical to github backend.\\n\\n5. **VERIFIED**: Both `docs/TASK_FILE_FORMAT.md` and `docs/sdlc-layers/layer-0/task-file-format.md` exist. `AGENTS.md` references `docs/TASK_FILE_FORMAT.md` at lines 115 and 409 as required reading.\\n\\n6. **VERIFIED (MERGED)**: All four PRs are MERGED: #3159 (replace plan-file authoring model), #3161 (scope write strategy), #3137 (correct swarm-task-planner description), #3156 (register architecture specs as artifacts). Recent git history shows commits from #3159 and #3137 in the log.\\n\\n7. **VERIFIED**: `tests_backlog/test_high_level_storage_boundaries.py` line 79 in `test_sam_server_has_no_task_backend_routing()` asserts `\\\"task_file_path\\\" not in source` for the `sam_schema.server` module.\\n\\n8. **VERIFIED**: Current count: `grep -rli \\\"task file\\\" plugins/development-harness --include=\\\"*.md\\\" --include=\\\"*.py\\\"` returns exactly 57 files as of 2026-08-28.\\n\\n**Summary**: All eight claims verified. No refutations detected. The issue's factual foundation is solid \u2014 `task_file_path` is a live data contract in the context models and context backends, regenerating at three independent points (memory, github, beads backends), while documentation continues teaching the file-based model. The structural fix (sibling PRs) has been merged.\\n</div>\\n\\n## RT-ICA\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-08-28T12:23:52.026583Z</sub>\\n\\nRT-ICA Snapshot: File-based language for SAM tasks persists because the context-file key and AGENTS.md required reading still teach it\\nDate: 2026-08-28\\nGoal: Remove task_file_path from the shared SAM task model and its regenerating documentation sources, then sweep remaining agent-facing prose.\\nConditions:\\n1. Current full list of code consumers reading task_file_path across all backends and hook scripts | Status: DERIVABLE\\n2. Exact test fixtures/assertions asserting task_file_path presence or absence that need updating | Status: AVAILABLE\\n3. Whether any consumer outside plugins/development-harness depends on task_file_path | Status: DERIVABLE\\n4. Current location breakdown of the 57 remaining \\\"task file\\\" prose occurrences (post plan-side sweep) | Status: DERIVABLE\\n5. Whether beads.py's task_file_path fabrication (found this session, not named in original issue) affects the beads test suite | Status: DERIVABLE\\nAVAILABLE count: 1\\nDERIVABLE count: 4\\nMISSING count: 0\\n\\nScope sizing note: item self-describes as a recurring pattern (~6 months, repeated prose-only fixes that didn't hold), and this session's own verification already found scope beyond the original Impact Radius (beads.py fabricates task_file_path too, not named in the issue). Per analyze.md's escalation rule, sizing set to FULL (6 agents: impact-analyst, fact-checker, classifier, rtica-assessor, alignment-analyst, groomer) rather than the recurring-pattern default of STANDARD.\\n\\nWave 0 (technical-researcher) skipped: this is entirely internal repo code (no external library/API/ecosystem question), and the item's own Root Cause comments already carry exact file:line citations equivalent to Wave 0 output. Verified during this session: sibling plan-side problem already fixed via merged PRs #3159/#3161/#3137/#3156.\\n</div>\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-08-28T12:35:37.115666Z</sub>\\n\\n**VERDICT: READY for planning**\\n\\n**Reconciliation of Regenerating Sources**:\\n1. `.claude/rules/large-file-write-strategy.md` \u2014 **RESOLVED** (merged PR #3161: \\\"scope the write strategy by mechanism, not by agent name\\\"). No longer a live regenerating source. Remove from scope.\\n2. `task_file_path` field in `sam_schema/core/models.py:749` \u2014 **OPEN**. Live data contract requiring rename to structured address (plan/task fields already exist on ActiveTaskContext; consumers must read those instead).\\n3. `AGENTS.md` required reading routing to `docs/TASK_FILE_FORMAT.md` \u2014 **OPEN**. Must retire doc reference and route agent instructions elsewhere.\\n\\n**Conditions Verified**:\\n- All facts verified (fact-checker, no refutations)\\n- Scope boundaries clear (two active regenerating sources, one resolved)\\n- Structured-address fields pre-exist; this is rename-and-route, not from-scratch invention\\n- Impact radius mapped (three fabricating backends: memory, github, beads; one consumer: task_status_hook)\\n- `docs/sdlc-layers/layer-0/task-file-format.md` confirmed as redirect stub; no deletion required\\n\\n**No missing preconditions for planning. Ready to proceed.** Recommend sequential ordering per closing hypothesis: (1) rename field + test fixtures, (2) retire TASK_FILE_FORMAT.md from AGENTS.md, (3) audit `.claude/rules` (already resolved but verify scope), (4) sweep prose.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Issue Classification\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-08-28T12:28:23.265437Z</sub>\\n\\n**Type: recurring-pattern**\\n\\n**Rationale**: Item explicitly documents ~6 months of repeated prose-only corrections that fail to close the issue. Each fix is followed by reintroduction of the same problem class, fitting the recurring-pattern definition.\\n\\n**Analysis Method**: Structural source inventory (performed during grooming). Identified two independent regenerating sources:\\n1. `task_file_path` JSON key in the SAM context-file contract (live data payload)\\n2. `AGENTS.md` \u2192 `TASK_FILE_FORMAT.md` required reading (agent instruction chain)\\n3. `.claude/rules/large-file-write-strategy.md` teaching plan-file model (repo-level rule)\\n\\n**Frequency**: Specific fix attempts not tracked in resolved backlog history (n=1 resolved items in GitHub backend, insufficient for historical overlap analysis). However, the issue's own narrative provides direct evidence: 138 current occurrences of file-based language (92 markdown, 46 Python) across 6-month observation period indicates continuous regeneration despite repeated attempts at correction.\\n\\n**Scenario Target**: Agents writing or modifying agent-facing documentation (skills, agents, rules) after reading `AGENTS.md` or `.claude/rules/large-file-write-strategy.md` as authoritative sources. The agents' behavior is correct per the sources they read, but the sources teach a model the system does not use.\\n</div>\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-08-28T12:29:07.485649Z</sub>\\n\\n**Type: recurring-pattern**\\n\\n**Rationale**: Item explicitly documents ~6 months of repeated prose-only corrections that fail to close the issue. Each fix is followed by reintroduction of the same problem class, fitting the recurring-pattern definition.\\n\\n**Analysis Method**: Structural source inventory. Identified two independent regenerating sources:\\n1. `task_file_path` JSON key in the SAM context-file contract (live data payload)\\n2. `AGENTS.md` \u2192 `TASK_FILE_FORMAT.md` required reading (agent instruction chain)\\n3. `.claude/rules/large-file-write-strategy.md` teaching plan-file model (repo-level rule)\\n\\n**Frequency**: Issue's own narrative provides direct evidence: 138 current occurrences of file-based language (92 markdown, 46 Python) across 6-month observation period, indicating continuous regeneration despite repeated attempts at correction.\\n\\n**Scenario Target**: Agents writing or modifying agent-facing documentation after reading `AGENTS.md` or `.claude/rules/large-file-write-strategy.md` as authoritative sources. Agent behavior is correct per the sources read; the sources teach a model the system does not use.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Files\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-08-28T12:40:41.614668Z</sub>\\n\\n**Structural sources (the two regenerating sources named in Root Cause):**\\n- `sam_schema/core/models.py:749` \u2014 `ActiveTaskContext.task_file_path`\\n- `AGENTS.md` (lines 115, 398, 409, 445, 468) \u2014 Required Reading routing\\n\\n**Fabricating backends:**\\n- `sam_schema/core/backends/memory_context_backend.py:59`\\n- `sam_schema/core/backends/github_context_backend.py:181,350-363`\\n- `sam_schema/core/backends/beads.py:1306,1378-1389`\\n\\n**Live consumer / dispatch:**\\n- `skills/implementation-manager/scripts/task_status_hook.py:322,363,457-468,714,729`\\n- `skills/implementation-manager/scripts/implementation_manager.py:1354-1371`\\n- `hooks/hooks.json` (PostToolUse + SubagentStop wiring \u2014 verify, not edit)\\n\\n**Tests exercising the field:**\\n- `tests/test_task_status_hook.py`\\n- `tests_backlog/test_task_status_hook_beads.py`\\n- `tests/test_dh_paths_integration.py`\\n- `sam_schema/tests/test_parent_issue_number_widening.py`\\n- `tests_backlog/test_high_level_storage_boundaries.py` (generalize beyond `sam_schema/server.py`)\\n\\n**Documentation (canonical + linking docs):**\\n- `docs/TASK_FILE_FORMAT.md` (retirement target)\\n- 10 docs linking to it: `docs/backend-providers.md`, `docs/backlog-item-lifecycle.md`, `docs/backlog-lifecycle.md`, `docs/workflow-architecture-diagram.md`, `docs/beads-and-workflow-usage.md`, `docs/plans/prd-workflow-extractor.md`, `docs/plan-artifact-lifecycle.md`, `docs/sdlc-layers/layer-0/README.md`, `skills/evaluate-sdlc-layers/SKILL.md`, `skills/dh-meta-docs/references/artifact-conventions.md`, `skills/dh-meta-docs/references/default-development-flow.md`\\n\\n**Remaining in-scope prose (~43 files, full list in this item's Impact Radius section):** 5 `agents/*.md` files (`code-reviewer.md`, `dh-context-gathering.md`, `feature-verifier.md`, `integration-checker.md`, `plan-validator.md`); 9+ `skills/*/SKILL.md` files (`clear-cove-task-design`, `dh-meta-docs`, `dispatch`, `execution`, `final-verification`, `forensic-review`, `generate-task`, `implementation-manager`, `interop`, `start-task`); `skills/backlog/references/item-schema.md`; `skills/work-backlog-item/references/workflows/work/interactive-browser.md`; `CONTEXT.md`; `README.md`; `docs/backlog-lifecycle.draft.md`; `docs/complexity-fit-and-economics-of-agents.md`; `docs/sdlc-layers/layer-1/layer-1-overview.md`; `docs/workflow-layers/KNOWN_ENTITIES.md`; `skills/dh-meta-docs/references/language-manifest-schema.md`.\\n\\n**Explicitly excluded from any sweep:**\\n- `local_context_backend.py`, `writers/yaml_writer.py`, `readers/*` and their tests (genuinely file-based, correct as-is)\\n- `migrate_tasks_to_github.py` and its tests/fixtures (legacy-format migration by design)\\n- `docs/sdlc-layers/layer-0/task-file-format.md` (confirmed redirect stub \u2014 no action)\\n- `.claude/rules/large-file-write-strategy.md` (already resolved via merged PR #3161 \u2014 not part of this item's scope)\\n</div>\\n\\n## Resources\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-08-28T12:40:41.614685Z</sub>\\n\\n- This item's own Impact Radius, Fact-Check, RT-ICA, Issue Classification, and Design Intent Alignment sections (#3151) \u2014 full structural analysis with file:line citations\\n- Feature-context discovery artifact: `plan/feature-context-sam-task-file-language.md`\\n- Related closed item #3261 \u2014 already fixed the dh-context-gathering/context-refinement side of this same description drift\\n- Adjacent open item #3141 \u2014 same theme, not superseded by this work\\n- Merged PRs that already fixed the sibling plan-side (not task-side) version of this problem: #3159, #3161, #3137, #3156\\n</div>\\n\\n## Impact\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-08-28T12:40:41.614594Z</sub>\\n\\nEvery agent that completes `/dh:start-task`, is dispatched as a task-worker, or edits agent-facing documentation is affected, because the session-context payload and `AGENTS.md`'s required reading are both in that path.\\n\\nConcrete consequences already observed: `skills/forensic-review/SKILL.md` documents a parameter named `task_file_path`; `skills/backlog/references/item-schema.md` defines the `plan` field as \\\"relative path to SAM task file\\\"; `skills/execution/SKILL.md` has a workflow step \\\"Read Task File\\\"; `agents/code-reviewer.md` names the right MCP operation (`mcp__plugin_dh_sam__sam_task`) but the wrong noun. Nine `skills/*/SKILL.md` files and five `agents/*.md` files still teach the file model directly.\\n\\nBeyond documentation, a path-based handoff silently produces an empty read in a worktree-isolated dispatch rather than an error, and on a remote (non-local-YAML) backend there is no file to read at all \u2014 so the miscommunication also carries a latent silent-failure risk, not only a training-signal cost.\\n\\nScope is confirmed at three fabricating backends (memory, github, beads context backends) plus one live consumer (`task_status_hook.py`, wired into both `PostToolUse` and `SubagentStop` via `hooks/hooks.json`) \u2014 every task-worker completion round-trips through this field today.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Impact Radius\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-08-28T12:30:04.520765Z</sub>\\n\\nSCOPE_EXPANSION: Original issue named two fabricating ContextBackend implementations (memory, github). This session's verification confirms a third \u2014 `sam_schema/core/backends/beads.py` (lines 1306, 1378, via `_resolve_task_file_path`) \u2014 and surfaces a fourth angle: `sam_schema/core/query.py` is a protocol-layer module whose docstring and API shape (\\\"Query layer for SAM task/plan files... delegate writes to the YAML writer\\\") teach the file model and is imported directly by two non-file backends (`beads.py`, `memory.py`) \u2014 though verified as docstring/scoping risk only, not active fabrication (see Code Other References). This session also REFUTES one claim in the original issue: `docs/sdlc-layers/layer-0/task-file-format.md` is not an active duplicate of `TASK_FILE_FORMAT.md` \u2014 it is already a 7-line redirect stub to the canonical doc (consolidated 2026-03-31). \\\"Delete the layer-0 duplicate\\\" should be dropped from the fix ordering; nothing to delete.\\n\\n## Code Producers\\n\\n- `sam_schema/core/models.py:749` \u2014 `ActiveTaskContext.task_file_path: str` (required), the root-cause field. Docstring: \\\"Session-to-task binding stored in context_dir() as active-task-{session_id}.json. The SubagentStop hook reads this file directly from the filesystem.\\\" The model already carries additive `plan: str | None` and `task: str | None` fields described as \\\"Plan address (structured address)\\\" \u2014 a rename target already exists on the model; this is not a from-scratch schema design.\\n- `sam_schema/core/backends/local_context_backend.py:72,128` \u2014 genuine file path via `_resolve_task_file_path`. Legitimate; excluded from sweep.\\n- `sam_schema/core/backends/memory_context_backend.py:59` \u2014 fabricates `f\\\"{plan_dir}/{plan}.yaml\\\"`.\\n- `sam_schema/core/backends/github_context_backend.py:181,350` \u2014 fabricates via `_resolve_task_file_path`.\\n- `sam_schema/core/backends/beads.py:1306,1378` \u2014 fabricates via `_resolve_task_file_path` (SCOPE_EXPANSION \u2014 not named in original issue).\\n- `skills/implementation-manager/scripts/implementation_manager.py:1354-1371` \u2014 accepts `task_file_path` as a function parameter, derives `plan_ref` via `plan_id_from_path()`, constructs `LocalYamlTaskProvider(task_file_path.parent)`.\\n\\n## Code Consumers\\n\\n- `skills/implementation-manager/scripts/task_status_hook.py:322,363,457-468,714,729` \u2014 reads `context_data[\\\"task_file_path\\\"]` / `active[\\\"task_file_path\\\"]`, derives the plan address via regex on the path string (`_extract_plan_addr_from_path`). This is the actual \\\"SubagentStop hook\\\" the model docstring refers to.\\n- `hooks/hooks.json` \u2014 wires `task_status_hook.py` into `PostToolUse` (matcher `Write|Edit|Bash`) and `SubagentStop` (matcher `^task-worker$`, 60s timeout). This is the live dispatch path, not documentation \u2014 every task-worker completion round-trips through this field today.\\n- Four test files exercise the field with literal fixture values, confirming the item's count: `tests/test_task_status_hook.py`, `tests_backlog/test_task_status_hook_beads.py`, `tests/test_dh_paths_integration.py`, `sam_schema/tests/test_parent_issue_number_widening.py`.\\n\\n## Code Other References\\n\\n- `tests_backlog/test_high_level_storage_boundaries.py:75-79` (`test_sam_server_has_no_task_backend_routing`) asserts `\\\"task_file_path\\\" not in source` for `sam_schema/server.py` only. The pattern is not applied to any backend module, so the field itself stays unconstrained everywhere else \u2014 this pins one clean module rather than closing the inconsistency. Candidate to generalize to backend modules once the field is renamed.\\n- `sam_schema/core/query.py` \u2014 verified NOT a functional leak into non-file backends. `beads.py` and `memory.py` import only the backend-agnostic `_new_plan_id()` helper from it; its file-reading/writing functions (`load_plan`, `update_status`, `create_plan_file`, etc.) remain used only by the CLI/MCP surface backing the local-YAML format. The risk here is that a \\\"core\\\" module's docstring and comments reason in file terms (\\\"Query layer for SAM task/plan files,\\\" \\\"Path to the plan file or directory\\\" x8+ in docstrings), which could mislead an agent editing this file even though its cross-backend blast radius is narrow. Treat as a documentation-tone fix inside code, not a structural one.\\n- `docs/sdlc-layers/layer-0/task-file-format.md` \u2014 confirmed 7-line redirect stub pointing to `docs/TASK_FILE_FORMAT.md`, already carries its own drift warning. No action needed.\\n\\n## Documentation\\n\\n- `docs/TASK_FILE_FORMAT.md` (577 lines) \u2014 the canonical doc slated for retirement per the item's fix hypothesis.\\n- 10 other docs link to it dire