ical artifacts were already excluded from this sweep; do not rewrite research history.\\n\\nAlso carrying forward architecture phase's review of the existing inventory:\\n- `implementation_manager.py:1354-1371`'s `task_file_path` is a DIFFERENT, unrelated CLI argument (local-YAML-only `claim_task` command; never reads `ActiveTaskContext`). It was listed under Code Producers alongside the real fabrication sites \u2014 flagged so it is verified/documented, not renamed by mistake.\\n- `sam_schema/core/models.py:737-745`'s docstring on `ActiveTaskContext` is itself inaccurate (\\\"SubagentStop hook reads this file directly from the filesystem\\\" \u2014 true only for the local backend; primary retrieval is the `sam_active_task` MCP call) \u2014 include fixing this docstring as part of the models.py task, not as separate polish.\\n- The layer-0 redirect stub (`docs/sdlc-layers/layer-0/task-file-format.md`) needs \\\"no action\\\" only pre-retirement. Once `docs/TASK_FILE_FORMAT.md` is actually deleted, the stub becomes a dangling link and must be addressed at that point \u2014 do not let a decomposition pass read the earlier \\\"no action needed\\\" note in isolation and skip this.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Dependencies\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-08-28T12:40:41.614702Z</sub>\\n\\nNo blocking dependencies. RT-ICA verdict: READY for planning (all conditions AVAILABLE or DERIVABLE, no MISSING). Design Intent Alignment verdict: MISSION_ALIGNED.\\n\\n- `.claude/rules/large-file-write-strategy.md`, originally suspected as a third regenerating source, is already RESOLVED via merged PR #3161 \u2014 not a dependency of this item, and not part of its scope.\\n- No dependency on adjacent item #3141 \u2014 independent, not superseded.\\n- Sequencing note (not a blocking dependency): the item's own analysis observes that prose corrections have no lasting effect while the two structural sources remain live, so the structural fixes are the precondition for the prose sweep holding \u2014 this is a scope-ordering fact for planning, not an external blocker.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Priority\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-08-28T12:40:41.614565Z</sub>\\n\\nP1 (already set). Justification: this is a confirmed recurring pattern, not a one-off \u2014 the same class of documentation drift has been corrected and has regressed repeatedly for roughly six months because two structural sources keep regenerating it. Every session that runs `/dh:start-task` or dispatches a task-worker touches the affected data contract and instruction routing, so the miscommunication compounds with ordinary use of the harness, not just when someone edits docs. RT-ICA verdict is READY and Design Intent Alignment verdict is MISSION_ALIGNED, so nothing about priority is blocked on missing information.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Benefits\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-08-28T12:40:41.614613Z</sub>\\n\\nOnce both regenerating sources are addressed:\\n\\n- Agents learn the actual backend-agnostic task address model (`P{id}/T{id}`) instead of a fabricated filesystem path, consistent across all four backends.\\n- The ~43 in-scope prose files can be corrected once and stay corrected, because nothing structural continues teaching the old model \u2014 closing a loop that has resisted six months of prose-only fixes.\\n- The existing single-module boundary assertion in `tests_backlog/test_high_level_storage_boundaries.py` can be generalized to guard all non-file backends, catching regression automatically instead of relying on repeated manual correction.\\n- Removes the latent silent-failure mode where a path-based handoff reads empty in worktree-isolated dispatch or has nothing to read at all on a remote backend.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Design Intent Alignment\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-08-28T12:34:44.102441Z</sub>\\n\\n**MISSION_ALIGNED** \u2014 This refactor closes a feedback loop between system architecture and taught model, directly supporting the harness mission of consistency and reliable delivery across sessions.\\n\\nThe proposed change aligns with the