eserves_concurrent_remote_revision` fails in isolation (`'queued' != 'revision-two'`) \u2014 confirmed unrelated to this feature's commits (no feature commit touches that test or the `GithubContentProvider` path), but it means \\\"full test suite green\\\" is not literally true for TN/T12 verification. Needs its own investigation as a pre-existing defect. (reported by qg-t2-sam-task-file-language on T2)\\n</div>\\n\\n## Root-Cause Analysis\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-08-28T12:28:23.265476Z</sub>\\n\\n**Primary Root Cause \u2014 Live Data Contract**: The `task_file_path` field in the SAM context-file JSON is a live contract key written by `/dh:start-task` and read by every agent and hook that accesses task context. Any consumer correctly interprets the field name as describing task files \u2014 the problem is structural, not semantic.\\n\\n**Regenerating Source 1 \u2014 Agent Instruction Chain**: `AGENTS.md` \\\"Required Reading by Task Type\\\" section routes task-related work to `docs/TASK_FILE_FORMAT.md` (29K, referenced from 10 documents, with a second copy at `docs/sdlc-layers/layer-0/task-file-format.md`). Agents read this as authoritative, learn the file-based model, then write that model into whatever they edit \u2014 in good faith and consistently with the live JSON key.\\n\\n**Regenerating Source 2 \u2014 Repo-Level Rule**: `.claude/rules/large-file-write-strategy.md` loads on Write operations and teaches the plan-file model (`PLAN.md`, `PLAN/` directory). It names `swarm-task-planner` as a canonical example implementing the 500-line policy. Agents editing planner content read the rule, see `PLAN.md` as current practice, and preserve it.\\n\\n**Propagation Pattern**: The file-based model has crossed plugin boundaries. At least three files outside `development-harness` teach it:\\n- `plugins/python-engineering/agents/python-cli-design-spec.md`\\n- `plugins/python3-development/agents/python-cli-design-spec.md` (duplicate)\\n- `plugins/python3-development/planning/sse-gap-analysis.md`\\n\\n**Why Prose-Only Fixes Fail**: Correcting the prose (138 locations) without renaming the `task_file_path` key or retiring `TASK_FILE_FORMAT.md` leaves both regenerating sources intact. The next agent to read and edit leaves the sources intact. The loop continues.\\n\\n**Closing Hypothesis (User-Provided)**: Structural-first ordering \u2014 (1) rename `task_file_path` to a plan/task address in the context-file contract, (2) retire `TASK_FILE_FORMAT.md` and remove it from `AGENTS.md` required reading, (3) delete the layer-0 duplicate, (4) audit `.claude/rules/large-file-write-strategy.md` scope and examples, (5) then sweep the prose. By that point, nothing regenerates it.\\n</div>\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-08-28T12:30:41.570418Z</sub>\\n\\n**Primary Root Cause \u2014 Live Data Contract**: The `task_file_path` field in the SAM context-file JSON is a live contract key written by `/dh:start-task` and read by every agent and hook that accesses task context. Any consumer correctly interprets the field name as describing task files \u2014 the problem is structural, not semantic.\\n\\n**Regenerating Source 1 \u2014 Agent Instruction Chain**: `AGENTS.md` \\\"Required Reading by Task Type\\\" section routes task-related work to `docs/TASK_FILE_FORMAT.md` (29K, referenced from 10 documents, with a second copy at `docs/sdlc-layers/layer-0/task-file-format.md`). Agents read this as authoritative, learn the file-based model, then write that model into whatever they edit \u2014 in good faith and consistently with the live JSON key.\\n\\n**Regenerating Source 2 \u2014 Repo-Level Rule**: `.claude/rules/large-file-write-strategy.md` loads on Write operations and teaches the plan-file model (`PLAN.md`, `PLAN/` directory). It names `swarm-task-planner` as a canonical example implementing the 500-line policy. Agents editing planner content read the rule, see `PLAN.md` as current practice, and preserve it.\\n\\n**Propagation Pattern**: The file-based model has crossed plugin boundaries. At least three files outside `development-harness` teach it:\\n- `plugins/python-engineering/agents/python-cli-design-spec.md`\\n- `plugins/python3-development/agents/python-cli-design-spec.md` (duplicate)\\n- `plugins/python3-development/planning/sse-gap-analysis.md`\\n\\n**Why Prose-Only Fixes Fail**: Correcting the prose (138 locations) without renaming the `task_file_path` key or retiring `TASK_FILE_FORMAT.md` leaves both regenerating sources intact. The next agent to read and edit consults the unchanged sources. The loop continues.\\n\\n**Closing Hypothesis (User-Provided)**: Structural-first ordering \u2014 (1) rename `task_file_path` to a plan/task address in the context-file contract, (2) retire `TASK_FILE_FORMAT.md` and remove it from `AGENTS.md` required reading, (3) delete the layer-0 duplicate, (4) audit `.claude/rules/large-file-write-strategy.md` scope and examples, (5) then sweep the prose. By that point, nothing regenerates it.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Second Regenerating Source Plans Not Just Tasks\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nThe description above covers SAM *tasks* being taught as files. The same loop runs independently for SAM *plans*, from sources it does not name \u2014 so closing the task side leaves this running.\\n\\n`agents/swarm-task-planner.md` creates plans through `sam_plan` (`create`/`append_task`/`finalize`) and never writes a plan file, yet its body still teaches a complete file-authoring model:\\n\\n- A \\\"Document Structure Policy\\\" prescribing a `PLAN.md` YAML frontmatter format whose keys \u2014 `description`, `version`, a `tasks:` list, `task_exports` \u2014 are fields on no SAM model, plus a `PLAN/` directory of per-priority part files for plans at or above 500 lines.\\n- A \\\"Large File Write Strategy\\\" section about a 25,000-character `Write` threshold for plan documents, task files, and `TASK/` exports.\\n- A \\\"Task Prompt Export Mode\\\" writing a `TASK/` directory.\\n- A \\\"Revision Management\\\" section instructing it to edit in place and never create `PLAN_v2.md`.\\n- T0/TN bookend task templates expressed as YAML blocks.\\n\\nThe regenerating source here is repo-level rather than plugin-level. `.claude/rules/large-file-write-strategy.md` loads on the relevant edits, names `swarm-task-planner` first in its scope list, and uses that agent's 500-line policy as its worked example:\\n\\n> **Canonical example**: The `swarm-task-planner` agent's 500-line progressive disclosure policy already implements Strategy A. Plans under 500 lines produce a single `PLAN.md`. Plans at or above 500 lines produce a `PLAN/` directory with `index.md` and per-priority part files.\\n\\nSo a rule that governs how any agent writes a large document teaches the plan-file model as its flagship illustration. An agent editing planner content reads that rule, sees `PLAN.md` presented as current practice, and preserves it \u2014 the same loop as `AGENTS.md` routing to `TASK_FILE_FORMAT.md`, one level up.\\n\\n### Plan-side inventory\\n\\nEstablished by reading the SAM backends and the callers, not by grepping prose:\\n\\n- `sam_plan` create/append_task/finalize persist through `sam_schema/writers/yaml_writer.py` into the backend's own plan directory. That is backend-internal storage, not a document an agent authors. No code path emits a `PLAN.md`, a `PLAN/` tree, or a `TASK/` export.\\n- `skills/add-new-feature/SKILL.md` Phase 4 is the planner's only caller. Its delegation prompt asks for the plan API and the returned plan ID, and names no file output.\\n- `task_exports` occurs outside the planner in exactly one place: `tests_sam/fixtures/nonstandard_frontmatter_tasks.md`, a negative-path fixture whose own notes state the canonical loader cannot parse that schema and that `tasks: []` in frontmatter raises \\\"No task entries found\\\". The planner was prescribing a format the loader rejects.\\n\\nContent still carrying the model, beyond the planner itself:\\n\\n- `skills/context-integration/SKILL.md` \u2014 instructs updating a Contextualization Status checklist \\\"at the bottom of PLAN.md\\\". The live equivalent is the plan's `context` field.\\n- `skills/task-decomposition/SKILL.md` \u2014 rules phrased against `PLAN.md` and `DISCOVERY.md` by name. The underlying rule (inline context rather than cross-reference) is live; the artefact names are not.\\n- `agents/t0-baseline-capture.md` \u2014 a \\\"Read Plan File\\\" step using a file read on a passed plan path. `agents/tn-verification-gate.md` reaches the same data through `artifact_read`. The two bookend agents disagree with each other about how the plan is reached, which is a live inconsistency rather than only stale wording.\\n- `agents/feature-researcher.md` \u2014 carries the full 25K Write strategy. This agent does still write a feature-context document, so whether the strategy applies to it must be checked before removal rather than assumed dead.\\n- `agents/codebase-analyzer.md` \u2014 migrated in substance (it states section appends have no single-call size limit) but retains a 25K-per-call figure.\\n- `plugins/python-engineering/agents/python-cli-design-spec.md` and its duplicate at `plugins/python3-development/agents/python-cli-design-spec.md` \u2014 both express the write strategy against `sam_create` and `sam_update`, tool names absent from the current SAM surface.\\n- `plugins/python3-development/planning/sse-gap-analysis.md` \u2014 states the planner produces `PLAN.md` and `TASK/` files.\\n\\nNote the last three are outside `development-harness`, so the plan-file model has propagated across plugin boundaries and one instance is duplicated between two plugins.\\n\\nTwo observations recorded rather than asserted:\\n\\n- Whether the 25K write strategy still has any reachable target for these agents after the API migration is not established here. If plans and artifacts are backend records, the threshold may no longer apply to the agents the rule names, which would make the rule's scope list stale rather than merely its example.\\n- `tests_sam/test_cli_migrate_fallback.py` and `tests_sam/fixtures/nonstandard_frontmatter_tasks.md` reference the file format. Migration paths legitimately need to read the old format, so these are not necessarily drift \u2014 the distinction between reading a legacy format and teaching it as current is what needs checking.\\n\\nOrdering consequence for the hypothesis above: the plan-side sources are `.claude/rules/large-file-write-strategy.md` and the planner's own body, and they are independent of the context-file key and `TASK_FILE_FORMAT.md`. Sweeping prose on either side alone leaves the other regenerating.\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"de689d1f9df35bcca33d1f7db50300e97f5c7200853529c61d38d3554a4416b9\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABRXcc1g\"}"}